remediation_fix:
Add a server_side_encryption_configuration block:
resource "aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration" "this" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.this.id
  rule {
    apply_server_side_encryption_by_default {
      sse_algorithm = "AES256"  # or "aws:kms" with kms_master_key_id
    }
    bucket_key_enabled = true
  }
}

Remove the public principal from the bucket policy. Replace
`"Principal": "*"` with specific IAM ARNs, or delete the policy statement entirely if public access was unintentional. Then enable all four
public-access-block settings:
resource "aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block" "this" {
  bucket                  = aws_s3_bucket.this.id
  block_public_acls       = true
  block_public_policy     = true
  ignore_public_acls      = true
  restrict_public_buckets = true
}

Replace the wildcard policy with least-privilege statements. List only the
actions the workload needs on only the ARNs it touches:
policy = jsonencode({
  Version = "2012-10-17"
  Statement = [{
    Effect   = "Allow"
    Action   = ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject"]
    Resource = ["arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket/*"]
  }]
})
Use IAM Access Analyzer policy generation from CloudTrail to derive the minimum set.

Enable deletion protection to prevent accidental destruction:
resource "aws_db_instance" "this" {
  deletion_protection = true
}
For S3, remove `force_destroy = true`. For EC2, set `disable_api_termination = true`.

Lock down the role trust policy. Replace the wildcard principal with the
specific IAM ARNs or federated providers allowed to assume the role, and add
a condition such as `aws:PrincipalOrgID` or `sts:ExternalId`:
assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
  Version = "2012-10-17"
  Statement = [{
    Effect    = "Allow"
    Principal = { AWS = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/DeployRole" }
    Action    = "sts:AssumeRole"
    Condition = { StringEquals = { "sts:ExternalId" = "unique-value" } }
  }]
})

If the load balancer must be internet-facing, attach a WAFv2 Web ACL and keep
listeners on HTTPS only. Otherwise make it internal:
resource "aws_lb" "this" {
  internal = true
  # ...
}

Replace the HTTP listener with HTTPS. Create an ACM certificate and attach it:
resource "aws_lb_listener" "https" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.this.arn
  port              = 443
  protocol          = "HTTPS"
  ssl_policy        = "ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06"
  certificate_arn   = aws_acm_certificate.this.arn
  default_action { type = "forward" target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.this.arn }
}
Add an HTTP listener that redirects to HTTPS (301).

Enforce IMDSv2 on the instance / launch template:
metadata_options {
  http_endpoint = "enabled"
  http_tokens   = "required"   # IMDSv2 only
  http_put_response_hop_limit = 1
}

Make the EKS API endpoint private:
resource "aws_eks_cluster" "this" {
  vpc_config {
    endpoint_private_access = true
    endpoint_public_access  = false
  }
}

